**Wrong way (leak risk):**
```java
Connection conn = ds.getConnection();
Statement stmt = conn.createStatement();
ResultSet rs = stmt.executeQuery(sql); // if this throws, conn never closed
conn.close(); // never reached on exception
```

**Right way (try-with-resources):**
```java
try (Connection conn = ds.getConnection();
     PreparedStatement ps = conn.prepareStatement(sql);
     ResultSet rs = ps.executeQuery()) {

    while (rs.next()) {
        // process results
    }
} // conn, ps, rs all automatically closed here — even on exception
```

try-with-resources works for any class that implements `AutoCloseable`. Connection, PreparedStatement, and ResultSet all implement it.

**Close order:** ResultSet → Statement → Connection (try-with-resources handles this automatically in reverse declaration order)
